<Legal title="Privacy Policy" heading="Privacy Policy" description="How Swarmnest collects, uses, shares and keeps personal information, including Stripe payments, Cloudflare analytics, email and your CCPA and GDPR rights." path="/privacy/">
<p>This policy explains how Swarmnest (owned and operated by J S in California, USA; "we", "us") handles personal information when you use swarmnest.ai, our API, our marketplace and our emails. We are the party responsible for your information (the "controller" under laws such as the GDPR). Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@swarmnest.ai">hello@swarmnest.ai</a>.</p>
<p><strong>The short version:</strong> there are no user accounts today, we do not run advertising trackers, we do not sell or share your personal information for advertising, and we collect only what we need to run the site, sell products and answer you.</p>

<h2>1. What We Collect</h2>
<h3>When You Visit the Site or Call the API</h3>
<p>Our hosting and network provider, Cloudflare, processes standard request data to deliver and protect the site: IP address, browser or client type (user agent), the page or endpoint requested, referring page, date and time, and approximate location derived from the IP address. Cloudflare uses this for security (for example, blocking attacks and bots) and gives us aggregated traffic statistics. This site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, a privacy-focused, cookie-free analytics service that measures aggregate traffic without tracking individuals across sites. We do not use Google Analytics, ad pixels or cross-site tracking.</p>
<h3>When You Email Us</h3>
<p>If you email <a href="mailto:hello@swarmnest.ai">hello@swarmnest.ai</a> (including to submit a tool, request a correction or takedown, ask about sponsorship, or ask about the waitlist), we receive your email address, name if you include it, and whatever you write.</p>
<h3>When You Join the Newsletter or Waitlist</h3>
<p>We collect your email address, the date you signed up, which form you used (newsletter or a product waitlist), your approximate country (from Cloudflare) and the wording you agreed to. This is stored in Cloudflare KV, our hosting provider's key-value store. We will ask you to confirm by email before sending marketing. If we use an email service to send the newsletter, it may record whether emails are delivered, opened or clicked, so we can see what is useful. We will name that service in this policy when the newsletter launches.</p>
<h3>When You Buy Something</h3>
<p>Checkout is handled by Stripe. Stripe collects your payment details, email address, and billing details such as name, country and postal code (and sometimes a full address or tax ID, where needed to calculate tax). We do not receive or store your full card number. Stripe gives us your name, email, billing country and postal code, what you bought, the amount, tax charged, and limited card details such as the card brand and last four digits. Stripe also uses device and transaction data to prevent fraud. Stripe's use of your information is described in the <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Stripe Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
<h3>Delivery Emails and Download Links</h3>
<p>After a successful payment, Stripe notifies our server. We create a download link that works for 72 hours and up to 10 zip downloads, store a record of the link (a random token, the product, the order reference, an expiry time and a download count) in Cloudflare KV, and email the link to the address you gave at checkout using Resend, our transactional email provider. Resend processes your email address and the message content to deliver it and may record delivery status. We also store a small order record (order reference, your email address, the product and whether the email was sent) in Cloudflare KV. Anyone who has the link can download the files, so please do not share it.</p>
<h3>When You Use the Search API or Download Files</h3>
<p>Our own code does not keep logs of search queries or API calls. Cloudflare processes the request data described above as our host. Queries are used only to return results.</p>
<h3>If We Add Accounts or Third-Party Sellers</h3>
<p>We would collect your login email, profile details and purchase history; for sellers, the identity, business, tax and payout information that we and Stripe need to pay you and meet legal obligations. We will update this policy before launching those features.</p>
<p>We do not intentionally collect sensitive personal information (such as health data, precise location or government ID numbers) from buyers, and we ask you not to send it to us.</p>

<h2>2. Why We Use It</h2>
