<p>We do not use your information for automated decisions that have legal or similarly significant effects on you, and we do not use personal information you send us to train AI models.</p>

<h2>3. Who We Share It With</h2>
<p>We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. We share it only with:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Service providers</strong> that process it for us: Cloudflare (hosting, security, analytics), Stripe (payments, tax calculation, fraud prevention), Resend (delivery emails with download links), our email provider for the hello@swarmnest.ai mailbox, and, once launched, our newsletter provider. They may only use it to provide their services to us.</li>
<li><strong>Creators</strong>, if we later open the marketplace to outside sellers: when you buy a creator's product, we may share your name, email and order details with that creator so they can support the product and meet their own legal duties.</li>
<li><strong>People who send copyright notices or counter-notices</strong>, as required by the DMCA process described on our <a href="/takedown/">Takedown page</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Authorities and others where the law requires</strong>, or where needed to protect rights, safety or the Service, such as in response to valid legal process.</li>
<li><strong>A buyer or successor</strong> if Swarmnest is sold, merged or reorganized, under a policy at least as protective as this one.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Cookies</h2>
<p>We do not set advertising or tracking cookies. Cloudflare may set strictly necessary security cookies, and Stripe sets cookies on its own checkout pages. See the <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Notice</a>.</p>

<h2>5. How Long We Keep It</h2>
<ul>
<li>Order and payment records: as long as needed for tax, accounting and legal purposes, generally up to 7 years after the purchase.</li>
<li>Emails and submissions: as long as needed to deal with them, and generally no longer than 2 years after our last contact, unless we need them for a legal claim. Copyright notices and counter-notices may be kept longer as a record.</li>
<li>Newsletter and waitlist: until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete your address. We may keep a minimal record that you unsubscribed so we do not email you again.</li>
<li>Download link records: removed automatically about 72 hours after they are created (they stop working at that time). Order records in Cloudflare KV (email, product, order reference): up to about 13 months, then removed automatically; Stripe keeps its own payment records as described above.</li>
<li>Request logs and analytics: held by Cloudflare for limited periods under its own retention practices; we keep only aggregated statistics.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
<p>Wherever you live, you can ask us to tell you what personal information we hold about you, give you a copy, correct it, or delete it, and you can unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time. Email <a href="mailto:hello@swarmnest.ai">hello@swarmnest.ai</a>. We will reply within 30 days (45 days for California requests, which the law allows us to extend once by another 45 days where reasonably necessary). We may need to confirm your identity, usually by asking you to reply from the email address we have on file. We will not treat you differently for using your rights.</p>
<h3>California Residents (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>
<p>California law gives you the right to know what personal information we collect, use and disclose; to delete it; to correct it; to opt out of its sale or sharing; to limit use of sensitive personal information; and not to be discriminated against for using these rights. You may use an authorized agent, and we may ask the agent for proof that you authorized them. In the last 12 months we have collected these categories: identifiers (such as email and IP address), commercial information (purchases), internet activity (request data), approximate geolocation derived from IP, and the content of messages you send us. Sources are you, your device, and our service providers. Purposes are those in section 2. We disclose them only to the recipients in section 3, for business purposes. We do not sell or share personal information and have not done so; see <a href="/do-not-sell/">Do Not Sell or Share</a>. We do not use or disclose sensitive personal information for purposes that would trigger the right to limit. We do not disclose personal information to third parties for their own direct marketing (California "Shine the Light" law).</p>
<h3>EU, EEA and UK Residents (GDPR/UK GDPR)</h3>
<p>You have the rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to our use of your personal information, to data portability, and to withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect use before you withdrew). You can complain to your local data protection authority. We are based in the US, so your information is processed in the US and by providers such as Cloudflare and Stripe, which use recognized transfer mechanisms such as standard contractual clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where available.</p>

<h2>7. Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
<p>We do not track you across other websites, so we do not change our behavior in response to browser "Do Not Track" signals. We treat a Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal as a request to opt out of sale or sharing; since we do not sell or share personal information, no further action is needed today.</p>

<h2>8. Children</h2>
<p>The Service is not directed at children under 13, and buying requires being 18 or older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 (or under 16 in the EU/UK without parental consent). If you believe a child has sent us personal information, email us and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>9. Security</h2>
<p>We use reputable providers, HTTPS throughout the site, and limit who can access personal information. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee security. If a breach affects your personal information, we will notify you where the law requires.</p>

<h2>10. Changes</h2>
<p>We will update this policy when our practices change, for example when the newsletter, accounts or third-party sellers launch, and change the "Last updated" date. For significant changes we will give notice on the site or by email where we have your address.</p>

<h2>11. Contact</h2>
<p>Swarmnest, owned and operated by J S, California, USA. Email: <a href="mailto:hello@swarmnest.ai?subject=Privacy">hello@swarmnest.ai</a>.</p>
</Legal>
